is centred and moves right. The colour decides it, and the pairs agree with each other every time:\n\n| colour | direction | pairs |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6 | up | 1, 2 |\n| 8 | right | 3, 5, 6 |\n| 4 | down | 4 |\n\n**Checking it.** Each output agrees with this table. Colour 6 squares end at rows 0–2. Colour 8 squares end at columns 7–9. The colour 4 square ends at rows 7–9. In every case the column or row along the other axis stays the same.\n\n**Applying it to the tests.**\n- Test 2 is colour 4, which the table covers. Its square moves down to rows 7–9 and stays in columns 4–6.\n- Test 1 is colour 3, which no training pair shows. I use \"left\" for it because that is the only direction the three known colours do not use. This is a guess, not something the training data proves. The square would end at columns 0–2 and stay in rows 5–7.\n\n**How the program builds the answer.**\n1. Clear the square from its old position and emit that canvas.\n2. Stamp it at the edge in its colour's direction and emit the final canvas.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    out = g.copy()\n    obs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n    dirs = {6: 'up', 8: 'right', 4: 'down'}\n    for o in obs:\n        for (y, x) in o[\"cells\"]:\n            out[y, x] = bg\n    emit(out, \"Lift the hollow square off the grid, leaving its old place empty.\")\n    for o in obs:\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        d = dirs.get(o[\"colour\"], 'left')\n        dy = dx = 0\n        if d == 'up': dy = -y0\n        elif d == 'down': dy = H - 1 - y1\n        elif d == 'right': dx = W - 1 - x1\n        else: dx = -x0\n        for (y, x) in o[\"cells\"]:\n            out[y + dy, x + dx] = o[\"colour\"]\n    emit(out, \"Slide the square to the grid edge given by its colour (6 up, 8 right, 4 down, other left).\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"In the output the square is the same shape and colour."}],"movement":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Which way it slides.** The position does not decide the direction."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Slide the square to the grid edge given by its colour (6 up, 8 right, 4 down, other left)."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Stamp it at the edge in its colour's direction and emit the final canvas."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"adc632168d5c2b96f369228a2e028705bd38b9b891c657eeaae7aec122db4d94","task_sha256":"85de1356e9068a56ee471b47846afd7d7c771d43586ab5815a7519fe78f47a74","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
